"RL FNA -
Absent colloid and scant follicular cells with oncocytic change showing mild architectural atypia. A repeat FNA after an appropriate clinical interval could be of benefit if clinically indicated.

"Retrosternal mass FNA - 
Scattered thyroid follicular cells arranged in a microfollicular pattern are identified in a background of scant colloid and blood. These findings include a differential diagnosis of hyperplastic colloid goiter nodule as well as a follicular neoplasm.

